# Table scroll and pinned pagination

A data table fills its panel. The toolbar and column header stay put, the rows scroll inside the table, and the pagination bar stays on the bottom edge of that panel. A side list in the same panel (category list, zone list) scrolls inside its own column the same way.

## Height chain

Every wrapper from the page section down to `DataTable` is a flex column that can shrink:

```tsx
<section className="flex h-full min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden">
  <div className="flex min-h-0 flex-1 flex-col overflow-hidden">
    <DataTable className="min-h-0 flex-1" />
  </div>
</section>
```

`DataTable` already grows with `h-full min-h-0 flex-1`, scrolls its rows, keeps the header sticky, and pins pagination with `shrink-0`. Do not add a min-height that makes the panel taller than the viewport.

## Lists

Give the list column `flex h-full min-h-0 flex-col overflow-hidden`. Put the rows in `ScrollArea` with `min-h-0 flex-1`. The header and search stay outside that scroll area.
